  "hardening_recommendations": [
    "Make mul_en assert unconditionally on every cycle of the 8-cycle sequence (cycles 1..8) regardless of the corresponding secret_operand bit value, and instead route the operand bit through an internal data-independent select/mask on the accumulator update path: when the bit is 0, perform a dummy add of a zero-valued (or otherwise non-informative) operand so that the accumulator hardware toggles the same way every cycle, eliminating the correlation between enable_count and popcount(secret_operand).",
    "Recode secret_operand internally (before the MSB-first bit-scan) into a constant-Hamming-weight representation (e.g. a fixed-weight code such that every encoded value has the same number of set bits), or use a two-share Boolean masking scheme where the multiplication is computed as the sum of partial products over masked shares whose individual activity patterns are independent of the true secret bits, so that per-cycle switching activity is uniform across all operand values rather than varying with the true Hamming weight.",
    "Note: merely adding random delay cycles after done, jittering the done pulse, or padding the transaction length does NOT address this leakage, since the enable_count/activity leakage occurs within the fixed 8-cycle active window itself and is independent of any post-done timing manipulation; only equalizing per-cycle switching activity (as above) closes this channel."
